.TH XD\-COMPOSITOR\-FX 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-compositor\-fx \- the XeonDesktop compositor with blurred Aero glass
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-compositor\-fx
.RI [ options ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-compositor\-fx
is
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
built on SceneFX's scene graph: in the Aero style it blurs what is behind
translucent glass (window frames, the taskbar, the Start menu) and draws
window shadows.
It takes the same options and reads the same files.
.PP
It needs a GPU renderer (OpenGL ES 2).
.B xd\-compositor
hands over to it on a GPU, so it is not normally run by hand.
Without a GPU it hands back to
.B xd\-compositor
with
.B XD_NO_FX
set, which draws in software and without blur.
It sets
.B XD_GLASS=1
for the session, which tells the shell and the other programs that glass
is blurred, so they draw Aero translucent.
.PP
It also draws the effects of Desktop Effects
.RB ( xd\-effects (1))
that need OpenGL, such as Wobbly Windows: a window an effect owns is drawn
into a texture and the effect draws it as a mesh, in the window's place
among the others.
.SH OPTIONS
As for
.BR xd\-compositor (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
As for
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
and:
.TP
.B XD_EFFECTS_TIMING
Set: while an OpenGL effect runs, how far apart frames are and how long
drawing them takes are logged every two seconds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR xd\-effects (1),
.BR xeondesktop\-session (1)
